stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> LIVE : record created and classified

    LIVE --> LIVE : still serving a live processing purpose
    LIVE --> ANCHORED : the class clock anchor is reached

    note right of LIVE
        Anchors differ by class.
        Register instance: the date of last entry
        after the instance closes.
        Employment record: exit.
        ICT log: creation.
        An unanchored record has no running clock.
    end note

    ANCHORED --> FLOOR_ELAPSED : min_retention for the class has run
    ANCHORED --> FLOOR_UNKNOWN : the floor is a counsel-set parameter with no value
    FLOOR_UNKNOWN --> FLOOR_ELAPSED : counsel sets the parameter and the period has run
    FLOOR_UNKNOWN --> ANCHORED : counsel sets a longer parameter

    ANCHORED --> HELD : RetentionHold placed
    FLOOR_ELAPSED --> HELD : RetentionHold placed
    FLOOR_UNKNOWN --> HELD : RetentionHold placed
    HELD --> ANCHORED : hold released, floor not yet run
    HELD --> FLOOR_ELAPSED : hold released, floor already run

    FLOOR_ELAPSED --> GATED : a conditional destruction gate applies to this class
    GATED --> ERASABLE : the gate condition is recorded, for example a transfer to a successor instance
    FLOOR_ELAPSED --> ERASABLE : no gate applies

    ERASABLE --> ERASED : deletion engine executes crypto-shred or tombstone
    ANCHORED --> CEILING_DUE : a ceiling class expires, purpose spent
    CEILING_DUE --> ERASED : erasure is required, not requested

    ERASED --> [*]

    note right of FLOOR_UNKNOWN
        An unset floor blocks automatic erasure
        and raises an unresolved-retention flag.
        It never defaults to zero.
    end note

    note right of CEILING_DUE
        A ceiling can fall due before a floor runs.
        Where they collide the record is retained
        and the collision is a counsel item, never
        a silent choice by the engine.
    end note
